        <div><h2 class="heading-title-mu" id="heading_0"><span>What is TOPIX ?</span></h2></div>
          <div>
  
            <div class="component-imgbox">
              <div class="component-imgboxL">
                
  <img src="/english/markets/indices/topix/tvdivq00000030ne-img/topix_logo_220401.jpg" title="" alt="" width="400" height="125">

              </div>
              <p class="component-imgText">TOPIX (TPX) is a market benchmark with functionality as an investable index, covering an extensive proportion of the Japanese stock market. TOPIX is a free-float
adjusted market capitalization-weighted index. TOPIX shows the measure of current market capitalization assuming that market capitalization as of the base date (January 4 ,1968) is 100 points. This is a measure of the overall trend in the stock market, and is used as a benchmark for investment in japan stocks.</p>
            </div>
          
</div>
    <div><h2 class="heading-title" id="heading_2"><span>Summary of TOPIX</span></h2></div>
          <div>
<div class="component-normal-table">
<table class="overtable">
<caption></caption>

<tr class="first">
  
     <td width="30%" class="a-center a-middle  tb-color003 fc-white">Index Name</td>
  
     <td width="70%" class="a-left a-middle ">TOPIX<br/>
 (Tokyo Stock Price Index, TPX)</td>
  
</tr>

<tr>
  
     <td width="30%" class="a-center a-middle  tb-color003 fc-white">Calculation Method</td>
  
     <td width="70%" class="a-left a-middle ">Free-float adjusted market capitalization-weighted</td>
  
</tr>

<tr>
  
     <td width="30%" class="a-center a-middle  tb-color003 fc-white">Start of Calculation</td>
  
     <td width="70%" class="a-left a-middle ">Jul. 1, 1969<br/>
The price return index is calculated and disseminated in real-time (per sec).</td>
  
</tr>

<tr class="end">
  
     <td width="30%" class="a-center a-middle  tb-color003 fc-white">Base Date / Base Point</td>
  
     <td width="70%" class="a-left a-middle ">Jan. 4, 1968 / 100 points</td>
  
</tr>

</table>
</div>
</div>
